                <pb facs="0149" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/768a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-20T18:00:00-05:00">March 20, 1930—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>54. You may emphasize the following: After conference with leaders, we are
                    convinced that present naval proposals to Japan are all it would be possible for
                    us to attempt to carry. Alternative is full twenty-three cruiser program.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
